From: WinterMist010 <85207868+WinterMist010@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] tu: fix a NULL dereference in tu_BindBufferMemory2() and a perf-query leak

Two independent fixes found while auditing the A8XX codepaths
(whitebelyash/mesa-unified#12).

tu_BindBufferMemory2(): memory == VK_NULL_HANDLE is a real case via
the VK_KHR_maintenance5 bind-status-query pattern, which this
function already partially implements.  It sets buffer->bo to NULL
and then unconditionally dereferences it in the following
vk_address_binding_report() call.  Guard the report.

tu_query_pool_destroy(): the derived-counter cleanup branch tested
is_perf_query_raw() a second time instead of
is_perf_query_derived(), so it was unreachable and every derived
query pool leaked its fd_derived_counter_collection plus the
hardware counters it reserved.

---
  src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_buffer.cc     | 8 +++++---
  src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_query_pool.cc | 2 +-
  2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_buffer.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_buffer.cc
index c7f70305c35..04e88e50e2a 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_buffer.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_buffer.cc
@@ -224,9 +224,11 @@ tu_BindBufferMemory2(VkDevice device,
 
       TU_RMV(buffer_bind, dev, buffer);
 
-      vk_address_binding_report(&instance->vk, &buffer->vk.base,
-                                buffer->bo->iova, buffer->bo->size,
-                                VK_DEVICE_ADDRESS_BINDING_TYPE_BIND_EXT);
+      if (buffer->bo) {
+         vk_address_binding_report(&instance->vk, &buffer->vk.base,
+                                   buffer->bo->iova, buffer->bo->size,
+                                   VK_DEVICE_ADDRESS_BINDING_TYPE_BIND_EXT);
+      }
    }
    return VK_SUCCESS;
 }
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_query_pool.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_query_pool.cc
index 70e6c9dfcea..f5a27c80a48 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_query_pool.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_query_pool.cc
@@ -301,7 +301,7 @@ tu_query_pool_destroy(struct tu_device *device, struct tu_query_pool *pool,
          if (perf_query->data[i].pass == 0)
             fd_perfcntr_release(device->perfcntrs, perf_query->data[i].counter);
       }
-   } else if (is_perf_query_raw(pool)) {
+   } else if (is_perf_query_derived(pool)) {
       struct tu_perf_query_derived *perf_query = &pool->perf_query.derived;
       struct fd_derived_counter_collection *collection = perf_query->collection;
 
